  "details": "TL;DR: If you don't rename the hand gesture animations after copying them from the VRChat SDK, VRChat will keep using the default ones\n\nHow to reproduce:\n\nIn a fresh Unity Avatar 2022 project\n\n1 - Copy the demo asset VRChat SDK animations and Gesture controller into the project (without copying the .meta, only the animation so that Unity recreates a fresh meta and id)\n\n-> vrc_AvatarV3HandsLayer\n\n-> proxy_hands_idle\n\n-> proxy_hands_open\n\n-> etc...\n\n2 - Customize the animations the way you want (bend the fingers, in a different way for example)\n\n3 - Replace all the animations with yours in the Gesture controller\n\n4 - Put your new Gesture controller in your avatar and upload it\n\n-> Your custom Gesture animations won't work and VRChat will still use the default Gesture animations\n\n6 - Rename your animations to anything else (custom_proxy_hands_idle, custom_proxy_hands_open)\n\n7 - Upload the avatar again\n\n-> The custom Gesture animations work again",
